%% 01-welcome.mgp - learn MagicPoint on gucOS, deck 1 of 10 (todos/0202).
%% What mgp is, where it came from, how to drive the viewer, and how this
%% tutorial series works. Teaches only directives the 0119 port renders.
%deffont "standard" tfont "/usr/share/fonts/mono.ttf"
%default 1 area 90 90, size 2, fore "white", back "MidnightBlue", font "standard"
%default 2 size 9, vgap 20, prefix " ", center
%default 3 size 5, fore "yellow", vgap 30
%tab 1 size 4, vgap 40, prefix "  ", icon box "SpringGreen" 50, left
%tab 2 size 3, vgap 40, prefix "      ", icon arc "gold" 50, left
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

Learn MagicPoint

deck 1 of 10: welcome

%center
%size 3, fore "gray70"
space / click: next page    b: back    q: quit
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

What is MagicPoint?

	a presentation tool for the X Window System
	written by the WIDE Project in Japan, late 1990s
	a fixture of unix and networking conferences
	its one big idea:
		a slide deck is a PLAIN TEXT file
		styled by lines that start with %
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

Why plain text?

	write slides in any text editor
	diff them, script them, keep them in git
	no binary format, no lock-in
	this whole tutorial is itself a set of .mgp files
		open any of them in an editor and peek
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

mgp on gucOS

	the viewer is /bin/mgp (the classic mgp 1.13a)
	double-click a .mgp file to present it
	right-click it, pick Edit: the TEXT opens
		that pair is the whole workflow
	freetype text; PNG, GIF and more for images
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

Driving the viewer

	next page: space, f, n, click, PageDown
	back: b, p, BackSpace, PageUp
	jump: type a page number, then g
		g alone jumps to the last page
	l redraws, q or Escape quits
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

The edit loop

	1. right-click this deck, choose Edit
	2. change some text, save
	3. back in the viewer, press ctrl-r
		mgp reloads the file in place
	that loop is how every deck here was written
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

The series

	02 your first deck        03 sizing text
	04 color                  05 alignment and areas
	06 lists and bullets      07 images
	08 backgrounds            09 builds and columns
	10 templates and mastery
%size 3, fore "gray70", center

work through them in order - each builds on the last
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

The end

%size 4, center
next: 02-first-deck.mgp
